Practical No. 12
Course Outcome: CO2
Aim: Write a program to count total nodes, leaf nodes and height of Binary Tree.
Theory: Several structural properties of a binary tree can be computed recursively. The total node count is 1 (for the current node) plus the counts of the left and right subtrees. A leaf node is one with no children, so the leaf count is obtained by recursively checking for NULL left and right pointers. The height of a tree is the number of edges on the longest path from the root to a leaf, computed recursively as 1 plus the maximum of the heights of the left and right subtrees.
Algorithm:
