Aim: Write a program to implement Bucket Sort.
Theory: Bucket Sort distributes the elements of the input array into a number of 'buckets' according to their value range, sorts each bucket individually (typically using Insertion Sort), and then concatenates the buckets in order to obtain the fully sorted array. It performs best (average O(n+k)) when the input is uniformly distributed over a known range.
Algorithm:
1. Create n empty buckets
2. For every element in the input array, compute its bucket index based on its value range and insert it into the corresponding bucket
3. Sort each bucket individually (e.g., using Insertion Sort)
4. Concatenate all buckets in order to produce the sorted array
5. Stop
